    hyperelliptic T-GEN to **one concrete group-generation hypothesis** over
    explicit loops — no covering scaffolding in the kernel.

- **Mathlib audit (correcting the route doc).** Mathlib *does* have the
  covering side: `IsCoveringMap.injective_path_homotopic_map` (π_* injective,
  Hatcher 1.31), `monodromy_bijective`, lifting criterion
  `existsUnique_continuousMap_lifts_of_range_le` (Hatcher 1.33). Gemini
  hallucinated a `fundamentalGroup_injective` name; the real one is
  `injective_path_homotopic_map`. So the residual narrows to **two**
  Mathlib-absent facts: (1) elementary index-2 kernel generation (even-word
  lemma over the parity monodromy ℤ/2; explicit gen set
  `{g₁²} ∪ {g₁gᵢ, gᵢg₁⁻¹}`), (2) branched puncture-filling van Kampen
  (`π₁(X∖T) ↠ π₁(X)`, kernel = meridian normal closure; `z↦z²` sends meridian
  to `g₁²`, filling kills `gᵢ²`, leaving the `2g` cycles).

- Prototyped (1) `ker_le_closure_parity` (scratch only, not landed): the
  `closure_induction` `mul`-case needs `Q=ℤ/2` pinned + the "two cosets" fact;
  ~2–4h of Mathlib group theory. Per the 90-min/sub-step discipline, NOT
  landed as a half-proof — no sorries introduced.

- **Per-family T-GEN status.** Hyperelliptic: T-GEN reduced to
  `BranchCutGeneratesPi1` (one hypothesis, the index-2 monodromy + puncture
